Z||000025||theogre||05-18-2000||12:09 AM||||late answer...... If FDISK only allows a 2 gig partition that's a BIOS and/or Chipset problem. The only way to eliminate it is to get a diferant MOBO. FDISK likely will only allow 2GB "logical drives" in the "extended" partition. (If it allows an extended partition over 2GB what it likely won't.)<P>All the "Socket 370" boards should take your hardware and CPU with no other changes. Then you could make the whole drive C: with partition magic. Some 370 boards may make you change memory some will take what you have.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 05-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000026||frontal lobe||05-18-2000||01:57 AM||||Ogre,<P>Thanks for getting back to me!  The bios did let me make a 4gig partition and allowed logical drive for all 4 gig.  When I look at the D drive in windows explorer it says it's 4 gig.  It all seems to be working.<P>I just got a copy of partition magic 2.0 from someone.  Should I leave well enough alone and keep running the way I am, or should I try out partition magic??||||reg||1
